// `<` is trait-backed (Ord). `String` conforms to `Eq` (`impl String as Eq`) but
// NOT to `Ord` — a collection/string has no intrinsic total order witness — so
// `str < str` must be a clean "needs an Ord witness" reject, not a blind byte
// comparison. (Since the removal of the structural Eq/Ord shortcut, every
// conformance is an explicit `impl`; String's missing `Ord` now fails the operator.)
fn main() {
    val a: String = "x"
    val b: String = "y"
    if a < b { }
}
